From de79aadfb36596d1dde4fc6397b99f12b6e40636 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:51:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] The Inner Garden, Phase 1: the gate opens, and your stone
 blooms

A members' portal at /members (one lazy, noindexed route, Disallowed in
robots.txt, left out of scripts/routes.ts and the shopper telemetry):

- The Gate for signed-out visitors: gold ironwork drawn from the Account
  sprig, three plain promises, Sign in or join (back to the room asked
  for), the Inner Circle form (source members-gate) and WhatsApp. While
  sign-in is being read the gate stays closed, with no signed-out flash.
- THE DOORS: the Naira flower draws itself in gold in the latch, petals
  burst, the leaves swing back (rotateY 100deg, perspective 900px) and a
  sage curtain lifts on its five-petal tassel while the garden blooms in.
  1.6 s once per IST day per device, 0.5 s after; a tap or key skips;
  nothing under reduced motion, where the heading takes focus.
- Her garden: a bed seeded from her user id (at most 80 plants, 24
  swaying, paused off screen, on a hidden tab and after 20 s idle) under
  a gold arbour, with the Naira flower planted the day she joined and her
  stone flower beside it; tap blooms on the bed and gate only (five at
  most, on the element, not window); "What's growing" as its text.
- Your stone: a first-visit seed ceremony with Skip; a birthday field that
  writes profiles.birthday through the existing row security; a specimen
  card that turns over (tap or drag) to the live Birthstone Heart Necklace
  with her month chosen by the listing's own variant name, live price and
  compare-at, Add to bag through CartContext, or Reserve on WhatsApp when
  sold out; every other month below, for a gift.
- Entry points: Account's COMING SOON preview-room panel becomes "Your
  garden"; /innercircle gets one static link; /auth replaces the Google
  button inside Instagram and Facebook's browsers with a note.
- A development-only preview member (?portalPreview=1) behind
  import.meta.env.DEV, absent from the build.

Isolation, honesty and IST tests guard it. The global CSS and the vendor
chunk build byte-identical to origin/main; the entry chunk grows by the
route rows (+87 B gzip); the route is 17.6 KB gzip JS and 3.3 KB CSS.

